the column is looked up in the internal \code{merge_field_table} (built from
\code{data-raw/merge_field_classification.csv}, which follows the NSSP ESSENCE
data dictionary) by its \code{\link[janitor:make_clean_names]{janitor::make_clean_names()}} name, then by a
looser spelling (lower case, no underscores) when that spelling points to
exactly one table row, so \code{c_biosense_id} finds \code{C_BioSense_ID}.
Anything else follows its type: text keeps both records' values
(\code{"concat"}), everything else takes the first informative value
(\code{"prefer_informative"}).
\item \code{merge_linked_episodes()} applies the rules to the rows of every
multi-row episode and returns one row per episode. The rules that need
